    <peripheral>
      <name>TIMER</name>
      <description>
        DesignWare APB timer (dw_apb_timer), 6 channels of 32-bit down-counters at a 0x14 stride
        (DS §4.8, p.187-200; Register Table 6 p.188-189). Checked against a live register read of a
        running DM-32UV (2026-09-27/28). Datasheet errors: Register Table 6 prints Timer5 and Timer6
        at 0x3c-0x4c (a copy of Timer4's rows) and §4.8.5.21-30 at 0x0-0x10 (a copy of Timer1's); the
        stride puts them at 0x50 and 0x64, where the live read shows Timer6 running and where the
        firmware accesses them (+0x50..+0x70). Datasheet field names are TimerEnable / TimerMode /
        TimerInterruptMask; this block uses enable / mode / int_mask. TIMERS_COMP_VERSION reads
        0x3230322a (DS p.200 and the live read). Channel 0 (TIMER_1) is the uC/OS-III tick: on a live
        radio LoadCount = 0xcd140, ControlReg = 0x03 (enabled, periodic, unmasked). It is PIC source 1,
        CPU vector 33 (DS Table 30). Confirmed on hardware 2026-10-01: with source 33 unmasked instead,
        the timer counted and held its line but nothing was delivered; with source 1 unmasked the ISR
        fired. Channel 5 (TIMER_6, source 6) drives the 10 Hz UI tick. Not the layout of QEMU's stock
        csky_timer device, which lacks the per-channel EOI/IntStatus registers (QEMU: dm32uv-qemu
        hw/timer/dm32_timer.c).
      </description>
      <baseAddress>0x14000000</baseAddress>
      <addressBlock>
        <offset>0x0</offset>
        <size>0x10000</size>
        <usage>registers</usage>
      </addressBlock>
      <registers>

        <cluster>
          <name>TIMER_CH</name>
          <description>Per-channel timer registers, 0x14-byte stride, 6 instances (Timer1..Timer6)</description>
          <dim>6</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x14</dimIncrement>
          <addressOffset>0x00</addressOffset>
          <register>
            <name>LoadCount</name>
            <description>Reload value loaded into CurrentValue on enable/underflow</description>
            <addressOffset>0x00</addressOffset>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>CurrentValue</name>
            <description>Live down-counter, counts down from LoadCount</description>
            <addressOffset>0x04</addressOffset>
            <access>read-only</access>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>ControlReg</name>
            <description>Timer channel control</description>
            <addressOffset>0x08</addressOffset>
            <fields>
              <field><name>enable</name><bitOffset>0</bitOffset><bitWidth>1</bitWidth><description>Timer channel enable</description></field>
              <field><name>mode</name><bitOffset>1</bitOffset><bitWidth>1</bitWidth><description>1=user/periodic mode</description></field>
              <field><name>int_mask</name><bitOffset>2</bitOffset><bitWidth>1</bitWidth><description>1=this channel's interrupt is masked</description></field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>EOI</name>
            <description>Read to clear this channel's interrupt (end-of-interrupt)</description>
            <addressOffset>0x0c</addressOffset>
            <access>read-only</access>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>IntStatus</name>
            <description>This channel's masked interrupt status</description>
            <addressOffset>0x10</addressOffset>
            <access>read-only</access>
          </register>
        </cluster>

        <register>
          <name>TimersIntStatus</name>
          <description>All-channel masked interrupt status</description>
          <addressOffset>0xa0</addressOffset>
          <access>read-only</access>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>TimersEOI</name>
          <description>Read to clear all channels' interrupts</description>
          <addressOffset>0xa4</addressOffset>
          <access>read-only</access>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>TimersRawIntStatus</name>
          <description>All-channel unmasked (raw) interrupt status</description>
          <addressOffset>0xa8</addressOffset>
          <access>read-only</access>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>TIMERS_COMP_VERSION</name>
          <description>DesignWare IP component version register</description>
          <addressOffset>0xac</addressOffset>
          <access>read-only</access>
        </register>

      </registers>
    </peripheral>

