    </peripheral>
    <peripheral>
      <name>Modem_Buffer</name>
      <description>Baseband RAM (DS §9.4/§10.4/§11.4, p.520-521, 555-557, 608). Two byte-wide RAMs of 1200 bytes: TX at +0x000 and RX at +0x4b0. Their layout depends on the mode. DMR physical layer: TX SEND_DATA0 +0x00-0x23 and SEND_DATA1 +0x24-0x47 (alternating frames), RX RECV_INFO +0x30-0x53. DMR link layer: PI/LC header, terminator or CSBK at +0x00-0x0b (Table 52). FM: 256-sample 16-bit PCM ping-pong buffers FM_VOICE_1 +0x030-0x22f and FM_VOICE_2 +0x230-0x42f in each RAM, high byte at the lower address. PSPEC also names MODEM_RAM at +0x960 and SOUND at +0x980 (not in the datasheet). The audio codec registers at +0x9c0 are described as the separate CODEC peripheral. FW: 8 byte reads at +0x32/+0x33.</description>
      <groupName>Modem_Buffer</groupName>
      <baseAddress>0x16000000</baseAddress>
      <addressBlock><offset>0x0</offset><size>0x4b0</size><usage>buffer</usage></addressBlock>
      <addressBlock><offset>0x4b0</offset><size>0x4b0</size><usage>buffer</usage></addressBlock>
    </peripheral>
    <peripheral>
      <name>CODEC</name>
      <description>Audio codec control registers, byte-wide (DS §6.5, Register Table 26, p.443-472; base 0x1600_09C0, inside the Modem_Buffer window). Mic inputs, DAC/ADC power and soft mute, digital mixer and AGC/DRC (the latter through indirect windows), gains, sample-rate selection and a countdown timer. Register names match PSPEC. FW: no access found by the movih scan (QEMU: dm32_codec logs named control writes).</description>
      <groupName>CODEC</groupName>
      <baseAddress>0x160009c0</baseAddress>
      <addressBlock><offset>0x0</offset><size>0x40</size><usage>registers</usage></addressBlock>
      <interrupt><name>Codec_interp</name><description>PIC source 37 (bit 5 of PIC_MASK_1/INT_ST_1), default CPU vector 69 (DS Table 30, p.168-169)</description><value>37</value></interrupt>
      <registers>
