    <peripheral>
      <name>PIC</name>
      <description>Programmable interrupt controller, 64 sources of which Table 30 assigns 38 (DS §4.7, p.166-187; Register Table 5 p.170-172). This is the chip's real interrupt controller, not the CK803S built-in VIC at 0xE000E100: the stock firmware makes no 0xE000xxxx accesses (program-flash sweep and live register reads). SOURCE vs VECTOR: source n is bit n of PIC_MODE/PO/MASK/INT_ST/FFLAG_L (n &lt; 32) or bit n-32 of PIC_MODE_1/PO_1/MASK_1/INT_ST_1/FFLAG_H, and byte n%4 of PIC_PRIOR&lt;4*(n/4)&gt;; the CPU sees it as vector n + PIC_VECTOR.vector0 = n + 32 at reset. Table 30 (p.168-169), source/vector: 0 reserved/32, 1 TIMER_1/33, 2 TIMER_2/34, 3 TIMER_3/35, 4 TIMER_4/36, 5 TIMER_5/37, 6 TIMER_6/38, 7 I2C1/39, 8 I2C0/40, 9 I2C2/41, 10 UART1/42, 11 UART2/43, 12 UART0/44, 13 UART3/45, 14 GPIOB/46, 15 GPIOA/47, 16 SPI0/48, 17 GPIOC/49, 18 PWM/50, 19 RTC/51, 20 SDIO/52, 21 USB/53, 22 SPI1/54, 23 SPI2/55, 24 LCSFC/56, 25 DAC/57, 26 ADC/58, 27 PCM_rd_data_interp/59, 28 PCM_wr_data_interp/60, 29 System_inter/61, 30 Time_slot_inter_tx/62, 31 Time_slot_inter_rx/63, 32 Rf_tx_inter/64, 33 Rf_rx_inter/65, 34 SlaveSPI0/66, 35 SlaveSPI1/67, 36 SlaveSPI2/68, 37 Codec_interp/69; all level-triggered, active high. CORRECTED 2026-10-10: the hand-maintained description this replaced listed CPU vectors as 'source assignments' (TIMER_1=33, TIMER_2-4=34-36, UART3=45, GPIOC=49, PCM_rd/wr_data_interp=59/60, System_inter=61, Time_slot_inter_rx=63, Rf_rx_inter=65, Codec_interp=69, and UART1/2/0=42/43/44, ADC=58, Rf_tx=64). Those are vectors; the sources are 1, 2-4, 13, 17, 27/28, 29, 31, 33, 37, 10/11/12, 26, 32. DRV's VECTOR_* defines (C7000_DRV.h: VECTOR_TIMER1-4=33-36, UART3=45, GPIOC=49, PCM_rd/wr_data_interp=59/60, System_inter=61, Time_slot_inter_rx=63, Rf_rx_inter=65, Codec_interp=69; bsp_vic.h: VECTOR_TIMER0=33, VECTOR_USB=53) are vectors too, passed to CKSetIsrVector, which unmasks bit (vector - 32); they agree with Table 30's vector column at every entry. The earlier note that a live trace's 'Time_slot_inter_tx = source 30' and DRV's 'Time_slot_inter_rx = 63' were an unverified TX/RX pair is resolved: Table 30 has tx at source 30/vector 62 and rx at source 31/vector 63. RTOS TICK: TIMER_1 (timer channel 0) is PIC source 1, CPU vector 33. Confirmed on hardware 2026-10-01 (OpenRTX bring-up on a DM-32UV, boot console log): with source 33 unmasked instead, the timer expired and held its line but nothing was delivered; with source 1 unmasked the ISR fired. The stock firmware registers its tick ISR with vector 33, stored at ISR-table index 33 - 32 = 1 (flash 0x0306cf70/0x0306cf38; dm32uv-qemu board-model notes (DM32-BOARD-MODEL.md), session 7). Register names and offsets also come from DRV bsp_vic.h ('Interrupt Controller definitions', Wang Huibin, 2013-05-13; in the DemoUV008 source tree at ucos3/include/bsp/bsp_vic.h), which agrees with Register Table 5 at every offset. Its CKIntcInit (bsp_vic.c) writes MODE = 0, PO = 0xffffffff, MASK = 0xffffffff, MODE_1 = 0, PO_1 = 0xffffffff, then MASK a second time where MASK_1 was probably meant, then INT_ST/INT_ST_1 = 0xffffffff. FW: 24 access sites in 2 code regions, all to MODE/PO/MASK/INT_ST and their upper-bank siblings; no access to PIC_VECTOR, PIC_COW1/2, PIC_PRIOR*, PIC_SYNC or PIC_FFLAG_* was found by the program-flash sweep, which does not cover IRAM (where the interrupt entry path runs).</description>
      <groupName>PIC</groupName>
      <baseAddress>0x17000000</baseAddress>
      <addressBlock><offset>0x0</offset><size>0x10000</size><usage>registers</usage></addressBlock>
      <registers>
        <register>
          <name>PIC_MODE</name>
          <description>Trigger mode select, sources 0-31. DS §4.7.6.1 p.172. FW: 0 reads, 2 writes. Bit n is source 0+n (sources 0-31). The datasheet prints one [31:0] field; it is split here into one bit per source named in Table 30 (p.168-169); bits with no assigned source have no field. Reset is all edge-triggered, while Table 30 requires level/high: DRV's CKIntcInit (bsp_vic.c) writes PIC_MODE = 0 and PIC_PO = 0xffffffff. FW writes this register (count above). Offset previously confirmed by DRV bsp_vic.h. Reset 0xffffffff (DS).</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0xffffffff</resetValue>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>Time_slot_inter_rx</name>
              <description>Trigger mode of source 31 (Time_slot_inter_rx, vector 63). 1: edge; 0: level. Table 30 specifies level-triggered, active high [reset 0x1] [access RW]</description>
              <bitOffset>31</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>Time_slot_inter_tx</name>
              <description>Trigger mode of source 30 (Time_slot_inter_tx, vector 62). 1: edge; 0: level. Table 30 specifies level-triggered, active high [reset 0x1] [access RW]</description>
