        <register>
          <name>PIC_MASK</name>
          <description>Interrupt mask, sources 0-31. DS §4.7.6.3 p.173. FW: 2 reads, 4 writes. Bit n is source 0+n (sources 0-31). The datasheet prints one [31:0] field; it is split here into one bit per source named in Table 30 (p.168-169); bits with no assigned source have no field. All sources are masked at reset. FW: irq_controller_unmask_and_register_handler @0x0306cf70 and sram_state_word_bit_clear @0x03001c50 take a CPU VECTOR v &gt;= 0x20 and clear bit (v - 0x20) here when v &lt; 0x40, else bit (v - 0x40) of PIC_MASK_1; DRV bsp_vic.c CK_VIC_EnNormalIrq does the same (bit irq_num - 32). So bit n here is source n, as the datasheet says. CORRECTED 2026-10-10: the hand-maintained entry this replaced said PIC_MASK covers sources 32-63 and PIC_MASK_1 sources 64+, reading the firmware's vector argument as a source number. Reset 0xffffffff (DS).</description>
          <addressOffset>0x8</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0xffffffff</resetValue>
