              <description>1: the CPU uses the vector number sent by the interrupt controller; 0: the CPU uses the automatic vector number 0x28 or 0x2c [reset 0x1] [access RW]</description>
              <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>priority</name>
              <description>1: use the per-source priority counters in PIC_PRIOR* (smaller initial value = higher priority); 0: default fixed priority IRQ0 &gt; IRQ1 &gt; ... &gt; IRQ63 [reset 0x0] [access RW]</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
