        <register>
          <name>PIC_INT_ST</name>
          <description>Interrupt request record, sources 0-31. DS §4.7.6.18 p.180. FW: 0 reads, 2 writes. Bit n is source 0+n (sources 0-31). The datasheet prints one [31:0] field; it is split here into one bit per source named in Table 30 (p.168-169); bits with no assigned source have no field. Write 0xffffffff to clear all records (DS §4.7.4.1 step 4). A 2026-10-09 firmware cross-reference found this word written all-ones at startup before the name was known, and DRV bsp_vic.h names it. Reset 0x0 (DS).</description>
