        <register>
          <name>PIC_MASK_1</name>
          <description>Interrupt mask, sources 32-63 (Register Table 5 prints 'Height 32', i.e. the high 32). DS §4.7.6.23 p.182. FW: 2 reads, 4 writes. Bit n is source 32+n (sources 32-63). The datasheet prints one [31:0] field; it is split here into one bit per source named in Table 30 (p.168-169); bits with no assigned source have no field. FW clears bit (v - 0x40) here for CPU vector v &gt;= 0x40 (same two functions as PIC_MASK). Hardware, 2026-10-01 (OpenRTX bring-up on a DM-32UV, boot console log): an OpenRTX build that cleared bit 1 here (source 33) read PIC_MASK/PIC_MASK_1 = ffffffff/fffffffd, the timer counted and held its line, and no interrupt was delivered; clearing bit 1 of PIC_MASK (source 1, TIMER_1) made the tick ISR fire. Named PIC_MASK_HI in earlier drafts until DRV bsp_vic.h gave PIC_MASK_1 (2026-10-09). CORRECTED 2026-10-10: the entry this replaced said this word covers sources 64+; it covers 32-63. Reset 0xffffffff (DS).</description>
          <addressOffset>0x68</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0xffffffff</resetValue>
          <fields>
            <field>
